Structure of HTML

<!doctype html>
  <html>
    <head>...</head>
    <body>
      <h1> This is heading.</h1>
      <p> This is paragraph.</p>
    </body>
  </html>

Explanation:

<!doctype html> = This line of code explain that we are using HTML 5
<html> = This is for html code, head, body and other tags, element come inside html.
<head> = This line is for heading, while we share any link the heading may be different that come here, the title of the article.
<body> = This tag hold body elements; like <h1>, <p>, <img>, <button>, <input>
Others closing tag represent that the end of body and html likewise head.
